samplax vendors kernels from the following JAX ports, released under the
Apache License 2.0 by the same copyright holder, and through them from the
original authors' code:

  - SGLD, SGHMC (with the v_hat noise correction), the HMC reference and the
    Gibbs Gamma hyperpriors: from SGHMC-jax
    (https://github.com/BoltMaxwell/SGHMC-jax), a port of tqchen/ML-SGHMC by
    Tianqi Chen, Emily Fox and Carlos Guestrin, "Stochastic Gradient
    Hamiltonian Monte Carlo", ICML 2014; SGLD itself is due to Welling and
    Teh, "Bayesian Learning via Stochastic Gradient Langevin Dynamics",
    ICML 2011.
  - Cyclical SG-MCMC schedules (cSGLD, cSGHMC): from csgmcmc-jax
    (https://github.com/BoltMaxwell/csgmcmc-jax), a port of ruqizhang/csgmcmc
    by Ruqi Zhang, Chunyuan Li, Jianyi Zhang, Changyou Chen and Andrew Gordon
    Wilson, "Cyclical Stochastic Gradient MCMC for Bayesian Deep Learning",
    ICLR 2020.
  - AMAGOLD: from amagold-jax (https://github.com/BoltMaxwell/amagold-jax), a
    port of ruqizhang/amagold by Ruqi Zhang, A. Feder Cooper and Christopher
    De Sa, "AMAGOLD: Amortized Metropolis Adjustment for Efficient Stochastic
    Gradient MCMC", AISTATS 2020.
  - Low-precision SGLD (full, naive and variance-corrected): from
    low-precision-sgld-jax (https://github.com/BoltMaxwell/low-precision-sgld-jax),
    a port of ruqizhang/low-precision-sgld by Ruqi Zhang, Andrew Gordon Wilson
    and Christopher De Sa, "Low-Precision Stochastic Gradient Langevin
    Dynamics", ICML 2022.

The original authors' repositories carry no license of their own. The ports
of Ruqi Zhang's code are released with the knowledge and agreement of the
authors (October 2026); the authors of ML-SGHMC were notified before release.
The methods, and the experimental designs they were verified against, belong
to their authors.

Two further constructions are implemented in samplax rather than vendored:
pSGLD preconditioning follows Li, Chen, Carlson and Carin, "Preconditioned
Stochastic Gradient Langevin Dynamics for Deep Neural Networks", AAAI 2016;
pCN-within-Gibbs follows Cotter, Roberts, Stuart and White, "MCMC Methods for
Functions: Modifying Old Algorithms to Make Them Faster", Statistical Science
28(3), 2013.

samplax was written with the assistance of Claude Code (Anthropic) for
Alberts, Bolt and Bilionis, "A path integral formalism for filtering and
smoothing stochastic differential equations" (2026). Full citation metadata
for the paper, the method papers and the source ports is in CITATION.cff.
